2	grid	sg_grid	\N	0.402000	kgCO2e/kWh	Singapore average Grid Emission Factor 0.402 kgCO2/kWh for year 2024. EMA verbatim: "Singapore average GEF decreased from 0.412 kg CO2/kWh in 2023 to 0.402 kg CO2/kWh in 2024." GEF covers all grid-connected generation including waste-to-energy and solar. NOTE: SEFR publishes Operating Margin, a different metric - do not substitute it.	EMA Singapore Energy Statistics 2025, Chapter 2: Energy Transformation, Grid Emission Factor. Verified 5 Aug 2026.	2024-01-01	\N
4	avoided	general_waste	recovery	0.111461	tCO2e/t	Avoided emissions basis: material diverted from incineration avoids exactly what incinerating it would have emitted. Equal to the SEFR incineration factor for the same material (other waste). Conservative - excludes any credit for displacing virgin material production.	Derived from SEFR (netzerohub.sg) incineration factor, other waste | NEA | 2006 IPCC Guidelines | AR5	2026-07-31	\N
5	avoided	paper_cardboard	recovery	1.530461	tCO2e/t	Avoided emissions for recycled paper/cardboard = the SEFR incineration factor for paper/cardboard, i.e. the incineration avoided. Conservative - excludes credit for displacing virgin pulp.	Derived from SEFR incineration factor, paper/cardboard | NEA | 2006 IPCC Guidelines | AR5	2026-07-24	\N
6	avoided	plastics	recovery	2.762461	tCO2e/t	Avoided emissions for recycled plastics = the SEFR incineration factor for plastics, i.e. the incineration avoided. Applies to PIL Cat A, recycled by Asia Recycling. Conservative - excludes credit for displacing virgin polymer.	Derived from SEFR incineration factor, plastics | NEA | 2006 IPCC Guidelines | AR5	2026-07-24	\N
7	avoided	metal	recovery	0.012461	tCO2e/t	Avoided emissions for recycled metal = the SEFR incineration factor for metal, i.e. the incineration avoided. WARNING: on this basis metal recycling appears almost worthless (metal barely burns). The real climate benefit of metal recycling is avoided virgin smelting, which this basis deliberately EXCLUDES. If that benefit is ever to be claimed, it needs a life-cycle source such as US EPA WARM and must be disclosed as a different basis.	Derived from SEFR incineration factor, metal | NEA | 2006 IPCC Guidelines | AR5	2026-07-24	\N
\.


